      "artist": "U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service Northeast Region",
      "description": "Pocahontas County, West Virginia, October 1, 2012.:  An original Shay engine #5 transport culverts to a fish passage project in a roadless area on Oats Run in Spruce, WV.  Oats Run is a headwater tributary of Shavers Fork that has native Eastern brook trout.  The culverts are part of a large-scale restoration project  to improve fish passage.  Cass Scenic Railroad is a partner in the project funded by the Eastern Brook Trout Joint Venture. The engine was once used to haul timber from Spruce, once a bustling town, but now abandoned.  Cass Scenic Railroad will haul all materials and heavy equipment via the rail line. Credit: Keith McGilvray/USFWS.",
